{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-qualified-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\" agent-context'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"contract\": \"TaskSpecAgentContext/v1\",\n  \"engine_version\": \"3.10.0\",\n  \"format_version\": 4,\n  \"default_format_version\": 3,\n  \"supported_format_versions\": [\n    1,\n    2,\n    3,\n    4\n  ],\n  \"binary\": \"taskspec\",\n  \"global_options\": {\n    \"--json\": \"wrap command stdout/stderr and exit status in one JSON envelope\",\n    \"--dry-run\": \"prevent supported mutations and report intended action\",\n    \"NO_COLOR\": \"disable ANSI color when present\",\n    \"TASKSPEC_COLOR\": \"0 disables and 1 forces ANSI color\"\n  },\n  \"exit_codes\": {\n    \"0\": \"success\",\n    \"1\": \"validation, gate, eval, or acceptance failure\",\n    \"2\": \"usage error\",\n    \"3\": \"unsupported runtime requirement\"\n  },\n  \"commands\": {\n    \"init\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"INIT=OK\",\n        \"INIT=DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec init [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\"\n    },\n    \"setup\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"SETUP=READY\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup | taskspec setup signing [--force] | taskspec setup decompose\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"setup signing\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup signing\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\"\n    },\n    \"demo\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DEMO=READY\",\n        \"DEMO=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"DEMO=BLOCKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec demo\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\"\n    },\n    \"example\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example task-plan --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\"\n    },\n    \"new\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec new [--format 3|4] [--status ready|blocked] [--queue] <slug> <XS|S|M|L|XL|XXL> [agent] [source-note]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--format\",\n        \"--queue\",\n        \"--status\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\"\n    },\n    \"plan\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_PLAN=OK\",\n        \"TASK_PLAN=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec plan --manifest <TaskPlan.yaml>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--manifest\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"batch\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_BATCH=OK\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec batch --plan <TaskPlan.yaml> | taskspec batch --intent-file <file> --effort <size>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--effort\",\n        \"--intent-file\",\n        \"--plan\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\"\n    },\n    \"migrate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec migrate <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\"\n    },\n    \"validate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec validate [--no-state] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--no-state\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\"\n    },\n    \"dod\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DOD=COMPLETE\",\n        \"DOD=GAPS\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dod <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"gate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TIER=1\",\n        \"TIER=2\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec gate [--stamp] [--require-tier1] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--require-tier\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\"\n    },\n    \"handoff\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HANDOFF=WRITTEN\",\n        \"HANDOFF=INVALID\",\n        \"HANDOFF=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec handoff <task-spec> --backend <token> [--out <file>] [--attempt-id <uuid>]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--attempt-id\",\n        \"--backend\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\"\n    },\n    \"run\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec run [--ci] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--ci\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\"\n    },\n    \"accept\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ACCEPTED=1\",\n        \"ACCEPTED=0\",\n        \"ACCEPTANCE_FAILURE=<code>\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec accept [--stamp] [--handoff <file>] [receipt flags] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--handoff\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\"\n    },\n    \"author-doctor\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=READY\",\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec author-doctor <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"holdout\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HOLDOUT=SEALED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=VERIFIED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec holdout seal|verify|run ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"receipt\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"RECEIPT=WRITTEN\",\n        \"RECEIPT=SIGNED\",\n        \"RECEIPT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec receipt validate|sign|engine|environment|evaluation|graded|human ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"eval-audit\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EVAL_AUDIT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec eval-audit <task-spec> --baseline <git-ref> [--mutations <matrix>] [--repeat N]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--baseline\",\n        \"--mutations\",\n        \"--repeat\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\"\n    },\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"IDENTITY=READY\",\n        \"IDENTITY=SIGNED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=VERIFIED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=REVOKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec identity init|sign|verify|revoke ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=VALID\",\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec evidence validate|plan|run <EngineMatrix.json> ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\"\n    },\n    \"bridge\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"BRIDGE=VALID\",\n        \"BRIDGE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec bridge export|validate ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"dsse\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DSSE=EXPORTED\",\n        \"DSSE=VERIFIED\",\n        \"DSSE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dsse export|verify ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"mcp\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"read-only stdio server\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mcp\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"read-only stdio server\"\n    },\n    \"mesh\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"MESH_WATCH_READY\",\n        \"MESH_SUPERVISED_ACCEPTED\",\n        \"MESH_FINISHED\",\n        \"TASKMESH_ERROR=<code>\",\n        \"TASKMESH_DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--execute\",\n        \"--initiative\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\"\n    },\n    \"ready\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec ready [--all] [filters]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--all\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"graph\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"GRAPH=<digest>\",\n        \"GRAPH=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec graph [--task <id>] [--check] [--mermaid] [--json] | taskspec graph --initiative <id> --view tasks|capabilities\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--check\",\n        \"--initiative\",\n        \"--json\",\n        \"--mermaid\",\n        \"--task\",\n        \"--view\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"NEXT=<command>\",\n        \"STATUS=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec status <task-id-or-path> [--json] | taskspec status --initiative <id>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--initiative\",\n        \"--json\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\"\n    },\n    \"lint\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec lint\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"transition\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"changes lifecycle status and derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec transition <task-id> <ready|in-progress|blocked|done|parked> [reason]\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"changes lifecycle status and derived state\"\n    },\n    \"rebuild-state\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec rebuild-state\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\"\n    },\n    \"archive\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec archive\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\"\n    },\n    \"backup\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec backup [destination-directory]\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\"\n    },\n    \"metrics\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec metrics [--since YYYY-MM-DD] [--author <name>] [--status <status>]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--author\",\n        \"--since\",\n        \"--status\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"conformance\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"self-test uses disposable fixtures only\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec conformance --self-test | --level L0|L1|L2 --executor <command>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--executor\",\n        \"--level\",\n        \"--self-test\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"self-test uses disposable fixtures only\"\n    },\n    \"executor\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"reference L2 executor; transitions, executes, accepts, or parks one supplied task\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec executor <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"reference L2 executor; transitions, executes, accepts, or parks one supplied task\"\n    },\n    \"agent-context\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec agent-context\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"completion\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec completion bash|zsh|fish\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"doctor\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"BACKLOG_DOCTOR=READY\",\n        \"BACKLOG_DOCTOR=BLOCKED\",\n        \"DOCTOR=READY\",\n        \"DOCTOR=BLOCKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec doctor [--backlog]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--backlog\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"version\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec version\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"help\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec help [command]\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"decompose\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose init|prepare|review|compile|status|impact|import <initiative> [options]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Native intent decomposition, signed topology review, and TaskPlan compilation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Native intent decomposition, signed topology review, and TaskPlan compilation.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"recipe\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec recipe list|show <strategy>|validate <file> [--budget <n>]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Inspect and validate resolved bounded execution guidance.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--budget\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"guide\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec guide <topic>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Read version-matched installed workflow guidance.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"decompose init\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose init <initiative> --intent-file <file|->\",\n      \"summary\": \"Create explicit intent workspace.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Create explicit intent workspace.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--intent-file\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"decompose prepare\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose prepare <initiative> --recipe <file> [--replace]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Validate and project an authored recipe; never approve it.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Validate and project an authored recipe; never approve it.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--recipe\",\n        \"--replace\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"decompose review\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose review <initiative> --accept --reviewer <name> --reason <text>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Authenticate explicit approval of the current topology.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Authenticate explicit approval of the current topology.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--accept\",\n        \"--reason\",\n        \"--reviewer\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"decompose compile\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose compile <initiative>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Compile reviewed topology and lineage without sealing leaves.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Compile reviewed topology and lineage without sealing leaves.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"decompose status\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose status <initiative>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Explain planning blockers and next valid action.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"decompose impact\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose impact <initiative> --against <bundle-or-snapshot.json>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Compare leaf projections to identify affected authorizations.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--against\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"decompose import\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec decompose import <initiative> --source <workspace>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Explicitly import originals; fresh native review required.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Explicitly import originals; fresh native review required.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--source\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"recipe list\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec recipe list \",\n      \"summary\": \"List available pinned strategies.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"recipe show\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec recipe show <strategy>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Show resolved guidance.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"recipe validate\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec recipe validate <file> [--budget <n>]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Validate a resolved recipe.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--budget\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"setup decompose\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup decompose \",\n      \"summary\": \"Provision locked dependencies in the private runtime.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Provision locked dependencies in the private runtime.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"receipt operational\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec receipt operational validate <file> | import <file> --out <path>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Validate or import operational evidence without upgrading its trust.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"Validate or import operational evidence without upgrading its trust.\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--out\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mesh init\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh init \",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh init operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh doctor\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh doctor \",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh doctor operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh serve\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh serve --foreground\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh serve operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--foreground\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mesh frontier\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh frontier \",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh frontier operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh run\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh run --task <id>|--frontier|--initiative <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>] [--provider <id>] [--mode supervised|autonomous] [--max-parallel <n>] [--execute]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Creates a run, worktree and lease; --execute starts the executor; --dry-run previews without creating them.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--adapter\",\n        \"--execute\",\n        \"--frontier\",\n        \"--initiative\",\n        \"--max-parallel\",\n        \"--mode\",\n        \"--model\",\n        \"--provider\",\n        \"--task\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mesh status\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh status [<run-or-attempt>]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh status operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"uninitialized status is read-only; existing runtime inspection may restart its daemon\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh watch\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh watch <run> [--after <sequence>]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh watch operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--after\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mesh explain\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh explain --task <id> [--adapter <name>] [--model <id>]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh explain operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--adapter\",\n        \"--model\",\n        \"--task\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mesh cancel\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh cancel <attempt>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh cancel operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh resume\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh resume <run-or-attempt> [--execute]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh resume operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--execute\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mesh accept\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh accept <attempt> --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh accept operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--reason\",\n        \"--supervised-by\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mesh finish\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh finish <run>\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh finish operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh adapters\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh adapters list|probe [<name>]\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh adapters operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"may initialize a missing daemon and write Git metadata; does not seal or accept tasks; probe invokes adapter executables\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh setup\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh setup sandbox\",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh setup operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"mutates TaskMesh state; never grants a TaskSpec seal\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"mesh mcp\": {\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh mcp \",\n      \"summary\": \"Use the existing TaskMesh mcp operation.\",\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"flags\": []\n    },\n    \"example task-plan\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example task-plan --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Write the installed task-plan example; existing output requires explicit --force.\"\n    },\n    \"example intent\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example intent --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Write the installed intent example; existing output requires explicit --force.\"\n    },\n    \"example recipe\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example recipe --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Write the installed recipe example; existing output requires explicit --force.\"\n    },\n    \"example incident\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example incident --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Write the installed incident example; existing output requires explicit --force.\"\n    },\n    \"example release-evidence\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example release-evidence --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Write the installed release-evidence example; existing output requires explicit --force.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"contracts\": {\n    \"task_spec\": \"spec/schemas/task-spec-frontmatter.schema.json\",\n    \"task_execution_recipe\": \"spec/schemas/task-execution-recipe.schema.json\",\n    \"task_plan_provenance\": \"spec/schemas/task-plan-provenance.schema.json\",\n    \"task_plan_bundle\": \"spec/schemas/task-plan-bundle.schema.json\",\n    \"task_plan_snapshot\": \"spec/schemas/task-plan-snapshot.schema.json\",\n    \"task_plan_import\": \"spec/schemas/task-plan-import.schema.json\",\n    \"task_plan_lineage\": \"spec/schemas/decompose-task-lineage.schema.json\",\n    \"task_plan_review\": \"spec/schemas/decompose-delivery-plan-review.schema.json\",\n    \"task_decomposition_recipe\": \"spec/schemas/decompose-recipe.schema.json\",\n    \"task_operational_import\": \"spec/schemas/task-operational-import.schema.json\",\n    \"task_operational_evidence\": \"spec/schemas/task-operational-evidence.schema.json\",\n    \"task_plan\": \"spec/schemas/task-plan.schema.json\",\n    \"task_materialization_receipt\": \"spec/schemas/task-materialization-receipt.schema.json\",\n    \"task_handoff\": \"spec/schemas/task-handoff.schema.json\",\n    \"task_revision\": \"spec/schemas/task-revision.schema.json\",\n    \"task_graph_view\": \"spec/schemas/task-graph-view.schema.json\",\n    \"task_status\": \"spec/schemas/task-status.schema.json\",\n    \"receipt_subject\": \"spec/schemas/receipt-subject.schema.json\",\n    \"acceptance_record\": \"spec/schemas/acceptance-record.schema.json\",\n    \"acceptance_finalized\": \"spec/schemas/acceptance-finalized.schema.json\",\n    \"acceptance_failure\": \"spec/schemas/acceptance-failure.schema.json\",\n    \"evaluator_trust\": \"spec/schemas/evaluator-trust.schema.json\",\n    \"mutation_matrix\": \"spec/schemas/mutation-matrix.schema.json\",\n    \"provider_smoke_evidence\": \"spec/schemas/provider-smoke-evidence.schema.json\",\n    \"authoring_evidence\": \"spec/schemas/authoring-evidence.schema.json\",\n    \"evaluation_receipt\": \"spec/schemas/evaluation-receipt.schema.json\",\n    \"graded_evaluation_receipt\": \"spec/schemas/graded-evaluation-receipt.schema.json\",\n    \"human_acceptance_receipt\": \"spec/schemas/human-acceptance-receipt.schema.json\",\n    \"environment_contract\": \"spec/schemas/environment-contract.schema.json\",\n    \"environment_receipt\": \"spec/schemas/environment-receipt.schema.json\",\n    \"authorization_receipt\": \"spec/schemas/authorization-receipt.schema.json\",\n    \"engine_run_receipt\": \"spec/schemas/engine-run-receipt.schema.json\",\n    \"holdout_bundle\": \"spec/schemas/holdout-bundle.schema.json\",\n    \"holdout_descriptor\": \"spec/schemas/holdout-descriptor.schema.json\",\n    \"agent_contract\": \"spec/schemas/agent-contract.schema.json\",\n    \"a2a_artifact\": \"spec/schemas/a2a-artifact.schema.json\",\n    \"mcp_task\": \"spec/schemas/mcp-task.schema.json\",\n    \"taskmesh_api\": \"spec/schemas/taskmesh-api.schema.json\",\n    \"taskmesh_run\": \"spec/schemas/taskmesh-run.schema.json\",\n    \"executor_capability\": \"spec/schemas/executor-capability.schema.json\",\n    \"dispatch_decision\": \"spec/schemas/dispatch-decision.schema.json\",\n    \"run_lease\": \"spec/schemas/run-lease.schema.json\",\n    \"taskmesh_event\": \"spec/schemas/taskmesh-event.schema.json\",\n    \"taskmesh_view\": \"spec/schemas/taskmesh-view.schema.json\",\n    \"sandbox_evidence\": \"spec/schemas/sandbox-evidence.schema.json\",\n    \"credential_lease\": \"spec/schemas/credential-lease.schema.json\",\n    \"taskmesh_roster\": \"spec/schemas/taskmesh-roster.schema.json\"\n  },\n  \"credentials\": \"TaskHandoff and AgentContext never contain credentials; provider and model credentials remain external to core.\",\n  \"taskmesh\": {\n    \"api\": \"TaskMeshAPI/v1alpha1\",\n    \"commands\": [\n      \"init\",\n      \"doctor\",\n      \"serve\",\n      \"frontier\",\n      \"run\",\n      \"status\",\n      \"watch\",\n      \"explain\",\n      \"cancel\",\n      \"resume\",\n      \"accept\",\n      \"finish\",\n      \"adapters\",\n      \"setup sandbox\",\n      \"mcp\"\n    ],\n    \"mcp_tools\": [\n      \"taskmesh.frontier\",\n      \"taskmesh.explain_route\",\n      \"taskmesh.start_run\",\n      \"taskmesh.get_run\",\n      \"taskmesh.cancel_attempt\",\n      \"taskmesh.accept_attempt\",\n      \"taskmesh.finish_run\"\n    ],\n    \"authority\": \"TaskMesh leases, routes, observes, recovers, and integrates; only canonical taskspec accept may accept a task revision.\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/intent.md .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/intent.md .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/decomposition.md'","aggregated_output":"# Intent and evidence\n\nRead the workspace's agent instructions, `taskspec agent-context`, and current\n`taskspec status --initiative <id>` before continuing an existing initiative.\nFor small, understood changes, author one TaskPlan unit or use `taskspec new` directly.\nDecomposition is optional; never invent lanes to fill a template.\n\nFor a broader outcome, collect the desired observable result, evidence sources,\nconstraints, responsible owner, and unresolved material decisions. Use\n`taskspec example intent --out intent.md`, then\n`taskspec decompose init <id> --intent-file intent.md`. Standard input is accepted\nas `--intent-file -`. An incident JSON file can be the explicit intake source.\n\nResearch the repository and author the decomposition recipe. Evidence needs source\nidentifiers and exact digests for local files. Missing ownership, evidence, or\nmaterial decisions is a blocker to explain, not a reason to invent an answer.\nExternal information remains reported until independently checked. Store decisions\nin the recipe so another harness can recover them without conversation history.\n# Native decomposition and review\n\nUse `taskspec decompose prepare <id> --recipe <file>` to validate authored input\nand propose topology. `--dry-run` produces diagnostics without changing the plan.\nEach accepted seam owns one swimlane; each capability leg names an observable\nstate and proof; executable leaves own coherent done-conditions and bounded writes.\nSDLC stages are concerns on the work, not mandatory lanes.\n\nRead `tasks/.plans/<id>/delivery-plan.yaml`, proposed leg artifacts, and graph\nbefore recording explicit human review:\n\n```bash\ntaskspec decompose review <id> --accept --reviewer <identity> --reason <decision>\ntaskspec decompose compile <id>\ntaskspec plan --manifest tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\ntaskspec batch --plan tasks/.plans/<id>/task-plan.json\n```\n\nReview binds the complete topology through the repository HMAC key using the\nplan-review domain. Compilation and materialization do not seal execution.\nThe authored recipe, immutable snapshots, native TaskPlanLineage/v1, bundle,\nand existing materialization receipt retain the intent-to-leaf chain.\n\nBefore replanning, preserve the prior bundle path. Use `prepare --replace`, review,\ncompile, then `decompose impact <id> --against <prior-bundle.json>` to inspect\nchanged, added, removed, and unchanged projections. Relevant constraints, recipe,\ndependencies, proof, and source changes require renewed authorization. Unrelated\nsibling changes preserve the earlier snapshot for unchanged leaves.\n\nRecipe task fields may include `execution_recipe` (a strategy name),\n`shared_resources` (resource identifiers requiring serialization), and\n`proves_capabilities` (leg IDs this integration-proof leaf independently evaluates).\nAbsence of a proof leaf leaves a capability unproven even when all children are done.\n\nOptional `sdlc_stages` values are `plan`, `design`, `build`, `test`, `deploy`, and\n`maintain`. One leaf may carry several concerns; these labels never create lanes\nor replace required evals. Original intake text is retained in the review and\napplicable leaf constraints. Import rollback is tested before materialization.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat tasks/.plans/rate-limit/seams/*.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/steel-thread.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/decisions/*.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/intent.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat tasks/.plans/rate-limit/seams/*.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/steel-thread.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/decisions/*.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/intent.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\nname: Decision visibility\ndescription: Separates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Present a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\nconsumes:\n- allow-or-deny decision\nproduces:\n- visible reason\n- decision telemetry event\nowner: reliability-interface\nindependent_proof: Response and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Emit a metric without returning a stable reason\n  reason: Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\n  name: Decision visibility lane\n  owner: reliability-interface\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\n    observable_state: Denials expose a stable reason and matching decision telemetry\n    proof: The response reason and telemetry payload share one decision identifier.\n    requires:\n    - allow-or-deny decision\n    produces:\n    - visible reason\n    - decision telemetry event\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-decision-visibility\n      title: Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\n      goal: Make the request 101 decision explainable without turning telemetry into authority.\n      done_condition: The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-request-101\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/decision.py\n      - tests/test_decision_visibility.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: request 101 is denied\n        when: the response is created\n        then: it exposes the stable reason organization_rate_limit_exceeded\n      - id: B-2\n        given: the same denial decision\n        when: telemetry is emitted\n        then: it carries the same reason and decision identifier\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: The response exposes the stable denial reason\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k response_reason\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Telemetry carries the matching reason\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k telemetry_reason\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Response and telemetry share a decision identifier\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k decision_identifier\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: expose an unstable free-text reason\n        reason: clients and operators could not depend on it\n        instead: use a stable machine reason plus human detail\n      - action: let telemetry authorize the denial\n        reason: observation cannot cross the enforcement boundary\n        instead: emit only after receiving the decision\n      - action: omit decision lineage\n        reason: response and telemetry could not be correlated\n        instead: carry one decision identifier across both outputs\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive response adapter, telemetry event, and focused tests.\n      observability: response-to-telemetry correlation test pass count\n---\n# Decision visibility\n\nSeparates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nPresent a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nResponse and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Emit a metric without returning a stable reason** — Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\nname: Policy contract\ndescription: Separates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Define and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\nconsumes:\n- authored organization policy\nproduces:\n- validated policy document\nowner: platform-contracts\nindependent_proof: Invalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Treat the API handler as the policy boundary\n  reason: Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\n  name: Policy contract lane\n  owner: platform-contracts\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n    observable_state: Rate-limit policy documents are schema-valid\n    proof: Invalid limits and windows are rejected; required fields are machine-readable.\n    requires: []\n    produces:\n    - validated policy document\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-policy-schema\n      title: Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\n      goal: Give every downstream stage one validated policy contract.\n      done_condition: A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on: []\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n      - tests/test_policy_schema.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a policy with a positive limit and window\n        when: the document is validated\n        then: schema validation succeeds\n      - id: B-2\n        given: a policy with a zero limit or window\n        when: the document is validated\n        then: schema validation fails\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: The policy schema exists and parses as JSON\n        bash: test -f src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json && python3 -m json.tool src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n          >/dev/null\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Valid policy examples pass the schema tests\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k valid\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Invalid non-positive values are rejected\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k invalid\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: encode limits only in handler constants\n        reason: downstream resolution would have no versioned contract\n        instead: validate one explicit schema before resolution\n      - action: accept zero or negative windows\n        reason: enforcement semantics would be undefined\n        instead: reject non-positive values at the contract boundary\n      - action: couple the schema to one storage provider\n        reason: policy shape and persistence are separate decisions\n        instead: keep the schema provider-neutral\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive schema and its focused tests.\n      observability: policy schema test pass count\n---\n# Policy contract\n\nSeparates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nDefine and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nInvalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Treat the API handler as the policy boundary** — Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\nname: Effective policy resolution\ndescription: Separates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Resolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\nconsumes:\n- validated policy document\n- organization identity\nproduces:\n- effective policy decision\nowner: policy-runtime\nindependent_proof: A deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter\n  reason: Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n  name: Effective policy lane\n  owner: policy-runtime\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n    observable_state: Every organization has one effective policy decision\n    proof: Defaults and organization overrides resolve with deterministic precedence.\n    requires:\n    - validated policy document\n    produces:\n    - effective policy decision\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-effective-policy\n      title: Resolve one effective organization policy\n      goal: Make policy precedence explicit before request enforcement.\n      done_condition: The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-policy-schema\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/policy.py\n      - tests/test_policy_resolution.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a valid organization override\n        when: effective policy is resolved\n        then: the override and its provenance are returned\n      - id: B-2\n        given: no organization override\n        when: effective policy is resolved\n        then: the validated default and its provenance are returned\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: Organization overrides win deterministically\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k override\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Defaults resolve when no override exists\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k default\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Resolution returns policy provenance\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k provenance\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: hide precedence inside conditional request code\n        reason: effective policy would not be independently testable\n        instead: expose one deterministic resolver\n      - action: return a policy without provenance\n        reason: operators could not explain the enforcement decision\n        instead: return source and version with the policy\n      - action: silently invent a default\n        reason: missing policy is an ownership decision\n        instead: require a validated explicit default\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive resolver and focused tests.\n      observability: effective policy resolution test pass count\n---\n# Effective policy resolution\n\nSeparates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nResolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nA deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter** — Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\nname: Request enforcement\ndescription: Separates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Apply the effective policy to the organization request count.\nconsumes:\n- effective policy decision\n- organization identity\n- current request count\nproduces:\n- allow-or-deny decision\nowner: request-runtime\nindependent_proof: A boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Infer enforcement from emitted metrics\n  reason: Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\n  name: Request enforcement lane\n  owner: request-runtime\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n    observable_state: Request 101 is denied for a limit of 100\n    proof: Boundary tests allow the first 100 requests and deny the next request once.\n    requires:\n    - effective policy decision\n    produces:\n    - allow-or-deny decision\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-request-101\n      title: Enforce the effective limit at request 101\n      goal: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\n      done_condition: Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-effective-policy\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\n      - tests/test_request_101.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 99\n        when: request 100 is evaluated\n        then: the request is allowed\n      - id: B-2\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 100\n        when: request 101 is evaluated\n        then: the request is denied exactly once\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: Request 100 remains allowed\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_100\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Request 101 is denied\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_101\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: The boundary has no off-by-one drift\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k boundary\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: check the limit after allowing the request\n        reason: request 101 would pass through\n        instead: decide before forwarding work\n      - action: use telemetry as the enforcement source\n        reason: observation is not authorization\n        instead: return an explicit decision from enforcement\n      - action: share counters across organizations\n        reason: one tenant could consume another tenant's budget\n        instead: key state by organization and window\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive enforcement boundary and focused tests.\n      observability: boundary test pass count\n---\n# Request enforcement\n\nSeparates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nApply the effective policy to the organization request count.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nA boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Infer enforcement from emitted metrics** — Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n# Steel Thread\n\n1. [`LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID`](legs/LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID.md)\n2. [`LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED`](legs/LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED.md)\n3. [`LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED`](legs/LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED.md)\n4. [`LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE`](legs/LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE.md)\n\nThis is a derived critical capability path. It records ordering, not\nimplementation completion or dispatch authority.\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: decision\nid: ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nstatus: accepted\nowner: example-fixture\nrationale: 'The fixture follows the blueprint order: schema, effective policy, request 101 enforcement,\n  then visible reason and decision telemetry.'\n---\n# ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\n\nStatus: **accepted**\n\nOwner: example-fixture\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe fixture follows the blueprint order: schema, effective policy, request 101 enforcement, then visible reason and decision telemetry.\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: delivery-intent\nid: DI-RATE-LIMIT\ntitle: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\nclaim: proposed\nsource:\n  uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n  captured_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00Z'\n  sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\nsuccess:\n- A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n- Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n- Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n- The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\nout_of_scope:\n- Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n- Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\n---\n# Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n\n## Delivery outcome\n\nFor every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy, deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nThis artifact records a **proposed** claim. Its source, capture time,\nand content hash are recorded in frontmatter; the claim is not implementation\nevidence by itself.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
