{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/system-map.md tasks/.plans/rate-limit/proposed-graph.json'","aggregated_output":"# Rate-limiting steel thread (test evidence fixture)\n\nSynthetic evidence source for `rate-limiting-recipe.yaml`. It exists so the\nproving fixture has a real local file to hash, and so source verification,\ndigest mismatch, and tamper rejection can be exercised without depending on\na large binary document.\n\n## Steel thread order\n\n1. A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n2. Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n3. Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n4. The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Provider-owned usage metering is out of scope.\n- Production storage and deployment infrastructure are not selected here.\n\nThis file is fixture input. It is not documentation of shipped behavior.\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: system-map\nclaim: proposed\ncomponents:\n- Policy contract boundary\n- Effective policy resolver\n- Request enforcement boundary\n- Decision response and telemetry boundary\nexternal_dependencies:\n- Organization identity supplied by the host application\n- Time-window and counter state supplied by an implementation-selected adapter\nunknowns: []\nproposed_steel_thread:\n- LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n- LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n- LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n- LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\nobjections:\n- id: OBJ-METERING-SEPARATION\n  status: FIXED\n  summary: Metering was removed from the canonical steel thread and kept external.\n  owner: example-fixture\n  rationale: The accepted boundary decision leaves metering outside the four-leg proving path.\ncontentions: []\n---\n# System Map\n\n## Components\n\n- Policy contract boundary\n- Effective policy resolver\n- Request enforcement boundary\n- Decision response and telemetry boundary\n\n## External dependencies\n\n- Organization identity supplied by the host application\n- Time-window and counter state supplied by an implementation-selected adapter\n\n## Unknowns\n\n- (none)\n\nThis is a **proposed** map. The delivery-plan transformation must\nclose or gate every material unknown; it may not reinterpret this text as\nruntime proof.\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"TASK_GRAPH=READY\",\n  \"plan_sha256\": \"09cb242fff217acfd43a52388bcf67c42596a99d2c4c14202156b47009863a03\",\n  \"nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\",\n      \"title\": \"Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/decision.py\",\n        \"tests/test_decision_visibility.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"title\": \"Resolve one effective organization policy\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/policy.py\",\n        \"tests/test_policy_resolution.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n      \"title\": \"Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\",\n        \"tests/test_policy_schema.py\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"title\": \"Enforce the effective limit at request 101\",\n      \"seam_id\": \"SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\",\n      \"swimlane_id\": \"LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\",\n      \"leg_id\": \"LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\",\n      \"effort\": \"S\",\n      \"profile\": \"standard\",\n      \"done_condition\": \"Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\",\n      \"touches_paths\": [],\n      \"creates_paths\": [\n        \"src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\",\n        \"tests/test_request_101.py\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"edges\": [\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"from\": \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n      \"to\": \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends_on\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contentions\": [],\n  \"critical_path\": [\n    \"T-20260802-policy-schema\",\n    \"T-20260802-effective-policy\",\n    \"T-20260802-request-101\",\n    \"T-20260802-decision-visibility\"\n  ],\n  \"critical_path_mermaid_sha256\": \"5ca6564fc3a4130a4f4de657714b91b354f60038f0d2902e908e1c7bad005824\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
